      "extract": "One of the ultimate goals of the quantum ﬁeld theory (QFT) is the quantization of gravity. It is well-known that usual rules of quantization when applied to the Einstein Lagrangian for the gravitational ﬁeld do not lead to a ﬁnite theory in a sense that inﬁnities cannot be eliminated by means of regularization and renormalization procedures [1]. With the advent of supersymmetry and strings [2] there was the",
